{#
/**
 * @file
 * Renders the container Slate injects a form into.
 *
 * The fallback link sits outside that container on purpose. Slate replaces
 * everything inside the container it is given, so a link placed in there
 * disappears the moment Slate touches it - including when Slate clears the
 * container and then stalls, which is exactly when the link is needed. Keeping
 * it outside means the loader can always bring it back.
 *
 * It points at the canonical form URL. The embed URL returns JavaScript, so
 * linking to that would hand someone a script file instead of the form.
 *
 * The link and the status region both ship in the markup. The loader hides the
 * link as soon as it takes charge, which leaves it visible for a browser with
 * no JavaScript - where the embed was never going to load anyway.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - attributes: (Attribute) Attributes for the container, including the id
 *   passed to Slate as the embed's "div" parameter.
 * - canonical_url: (string) The browser-navigable form URL.
 */
#}
<div class="az-media-slate">
  <div{{ attributes }}></div>
  <a href="{{ canonical_url }}" class="az-media-slate__fallback" rel="noopener">
    {{ 'Open this form'|t }}
  </a>
  <p class="az-media-slate__status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</div>
